cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SSEE cosmology — Structural Self-Energy Expansion"
abstract: >
  A minimal-parameter dark-energy framework whose background is fixed algebraically
  from φ (golden ratio) and π, with two free parameters at CMB level {A_s, τ}.
  One matter sector, unmodified gravity. Ten papers: algebraic framework and
  Predictive Register; Bayesian comparison against DESI DR2 BAO; full Planck CMB
  likelihood; algebraic derivation of CMB observables; Israel-Stewart causal
  perturbations; growth sector against raw cosmic-shear (KiDS-Legacy) and BOSS
  full-shape data with the background held fixed; canonical EFT (ghost-condensate
  k-essence); strong-gravity regime; Hubble-tension screening cascade (SH0ES in,
  global H out); UV completion. Every number in the papers is generated from a
  logged run (DVC pipeline with provenance); see AUDIT.md and CANONICAL_VALUES.yaml.
  Open problems are listed in OPEN_PROBLEMS.md.
